Package: PeakGeneNet
Type: Package
Title: Integration of Epigenomic Peaks to Genes through Correlation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Anne", "Weitzel",
      email = "weitzela@umich.edu",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7615-6357")
    )
  )
Description: Links epigenomic peaks to gene expression through empirical
    Spearman correlation across multi-omic samples. Unlike annotation tools
    that assign peaks to the nearest gene, PeakGeneNet tests all peak–gene
    pairs within a configurable locus window (default 1 Mb) and applies
    FDR correction within biologically defined groups. Four link types are
    assessed: promoter peaks to genes, distal peaks to genes, distal peaks
    to promoter peaks, and promoter peaks to promoter peaks. Designed for
    multi-omic datasets integrating ATAC-seq, CUT&Tag, and RNA-seq, with
    support for any organism and genome build available through Ensembl.
